# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Leave BOTH of these unset and the app runs in local mode: no sign-in, the
# sample roster loaded, everything saved in the browser. That is what makes
# `npm run dev` work on a fresh clone with zero setup.
#
# Set BOTH and the app switches to real accounts: email sign-in, per-user
# clients and schedule, enforced by row level security in Postgres.
#
# Both values are safe to expose in the browser -- that is what the
# "publishable" / "anon" key is for. RLS is what protects the data, not key
# secrecy. Never put the service_role key in a NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable; it
# bypasses RLS entirely.
#
# Find them in: Supabase dashboard -> Project Settings -> API

# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://yourproject.supabase.co

# Newer projects show a publishable key (sb_publishable_...); older ones show
# an anon key (a long JWT). Either works -- set whichever one you have.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
